message: "If you use this software, please cite it."
title: "geotech-rl: a procedural reinforcement-learning environment for geotechnical judgement"
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Cunha da Silva"
    given-names: "Arthur"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-6285-6903"

doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23861866"
repository-code: "https://github.com/arthurcunha51eng/geotech-rl"
version: "0.1.1"
date-released: "2026-11-01"
license: MIT

abstract: >-
  A procedural reinforcement-learning environment built from a geotechnical
  decision: which lighting-pole foundations must be redone, given messy site
  records. It generates seeded instances with a physics-based truth, discards
  instances that a listed wrong route can solve, and trains a small open model
  with SFT and GRPO. All data is synthetic.

keywords:
  - reinforcement learning
  - procedural environment
  - geotechnical engineering
  - GRPO
  - AI evaluation
